From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] feat(Hardware Support): KONKR Pocket FIT system buttons

The Pocket FIT's gamepad MCU reports K, =, LC, RC and the right-side menu
button on a UART, in the same protocol as the Pocket FIT Elite. With the
konkr_sysbtn driver bound to it they arrive as "KONKR System Buttons"
(BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY1..5); take them as a source with the Elite's konkr3 map.
---
diff --git a/rootfs/usr/share/inputplumber/devices/50-konkr_pocket_fit.yaml b/rootfs/usr/share/inputplumber/devices/50-konkr_pocket_fit.yaml
--- a/rootfs/usr/share/inputplumber/devices/50-konkr_pocket_fit.yaml
+++ b/rootfs/usr/share/inputplumber/devices/50-konkr_pocket_fit.yaml
@@ -44,6 +44,13 @@
           vendor_id: 1c4f
           product_id: 0002
           handler: event*
+    # Extra buttons (K, =, LC, RC, right-side menu) from the gamepad MCU's UART,
+    # via the konkr_sysbtn kernel driver -- same events as on the Pocket FIT Elite.
+    - group: keyboard
+      capability_map_id: konkr3
+      evdev:
+          name: KONKR System Buttons
+          handler: event*
 
 target_devices:
     - xbox-elite
